#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure of the Java images (Edge, Backend, Backend-Edge)"
msgstr "Aufbau der Java-Images (Edge, Backend, Backend-Edge)"

#. type: #sec-structure-of-the-java-images-edge-backend-backend-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"All three Dockerfiles are built the same way and differ only in the Gradle "
"task, JAR name, ports and default JVM options."
msgstr ""
"Alle drei Dockerfiles sind gleich gebaut und unterscheiden sich nur im "
"Gradle-Task, im JAR-Namen, in den Ports und in den voreingestellten JVM-"
"Optionen."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stage 1: build"
msgstr "Stufe 1: Build"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ARG JAVA_VERSION=25\n"
"ARG JAVA_PACKAGE=jre\n"
msgstr ""
"ARG JAVA_VERSION=25\n"
"ARG JAVA_PACKAGE=jre\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM eclipse-temurin:${JAVA_VERSION}-jdk-alpine AS build_edge\n"
"RUN apk add --no-cache dos2unix bash\n"
"COPY tools/docker/edge/root/ /opt/root/\n"
"RUN find /opt/root/ -type f -print0 | xargs -0 dos2unix\n"
"WORKDIR /src\n"
"ENV OEMS_EDGE_OUTPUT=/opt/openems-edge.jar\n"
"RUN --mount=type=bind,target=.,readwrite \\\n"
"    --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.gradle \\\n"
"    ./gradlew --no-build-cache buildEdge\n"
msgstr ""
"FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM eclipse-temurin:${JAVA_VERSION}-jdk-alpine AS build_edge\n"
"RUN apk add --no-cache dos2unix bash\n"
"COPY tools/docker/edge/root/ /opt/root/\n"
"RUN find /opt/root/ -type f -print0 | xargs -0 dos2unix\n"
"WORKDIR /src\n"
"ENV OEMS_EDGE_OUTPUT=/opt/openems-edge.jar\n"
"RUN --mount=type=bind,target=.,readwrite \\\n"
"    --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.gradle \\\n"
"    ./gradlew --no-build-cache buildEdge\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**The build context is the root directory of the repository.** The source "
"code is not copied, but mounted via `+--mount=type=bind,readwrite+`. Write "
"accesses of the build (e.g. `+generated/+`) end up in a throwaway layer and "
"do not change the working tree."
msgstr ""
"**Build-Kontext ist das Wurzelverzeichnis des Repositorys.** Der Quellcode "
"wird nicht kopiert, sondern per `+--mount=type=bind,readwrite+` "
"eingeblendet. Schreibzugriffe des Builds (z. B. `+generated/+`) landen in "
"einer Wegwerf-Schicht und verändern den Arbeitsbaum nicht."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+--mount=type=cache,target=/root/.gradle+` keeps Gradle dependencies "
"between builds. This requires BuildKit."
msgstr ""
"`+--mount=type=cache,target=/root/.gradle+` hält Gradle-Abhängigkeiten "
"zwischen Builds vor. Das setzt BuildKit voraus (bei aktuellem Docker "
"Standard)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+--platform=$BUILDPLATFORM+`: the build stage always runs in the "
"architecture of the build machine, because the result is a platform-"
"independent JAR. Only the runtime stage is built for the target architecture."
msgstr ""
"`+--platform=$BUILDPLATFORM+`: Die Build-Stufe läuft immer in der "
"Architektur des Build-Rechners. Das ist möglich, weil das Ergebnis ein "
"plattformunabhängiges JAR ist. Nur die Laufzeitstufe wird für die "
"Zielarchitektur gebaut."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Gradle tasks `+buildEdge+`, `+buildBackend+` and `+buildBackendEdge+` "
"write their JAR to the path from `+OEMS_EDGE_OUTPUT+`, "
"`+OEMS_BACKEND_OUTPUT+` or `+OEMS_BACKEND_EDGE_OUTPUT+`."
msgstr ""
"Die Gradle-Tasks `+buildEdge+`, `+buildBackend+` und `+buildBackendEdge+` "
"schreiben ihr JAR an den Pfad aus `+OEMS_EDGE_OUTPUT+`, "
"`+OEMS_BACKEND_OUTPUT+` bzw. `+OEMS_BACKEND_EDGE_OUTPUT+`."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+dos2unix+` on the start scripts prevents problems if the repository was "
"checked out on Windows with CRLF."
msgstr ""
"`+dos2unix+` über die Startskripte verhindert Probleme, wenn das Repository "
"unter Windows mit CRLF ausgecheckt wurde."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stages 2 and 3: runtime"
msgstr "Stufe 2 und 3: Laufzeit"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FROM ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:edge AS base_container\n"
"... add the Adoptium APK repository ...\n"
"RUN apk add --update --no-cache rsync dos2unix temurin-${JAVA_VERSION}-${JAVA_PACKAGE}\n"
msgstr ""
"FROM ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:edge AS base_container\n"
"... Adoptium-APK-Repository eintragen ...\n"
"RUN apk add --update --no-cache rsync dos2unix temurin-${JAVA_VERSION}-${JAVA_PACKAGE}\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FROM base_container\n"
"COPY --from=build_edge --chown=abc:abc /opt/root/ /\n"
"COPY --from=build_edge --chown=abc:abc /opt/openems-edge.jar /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
"RUN find /etc/s6-overlay/ -type f -name 'run' -exec chmod +x {} \\;\n"
"ENV EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=\"-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError\"\n"
"VOLUME /var/opt/openems/config\n"
"VOLUME /var/opt/openems/data\n"
"EXPOSE 8080 8085\n"
msgstr ""
"FROM base_container\n"
"COPY --from=build_edge --chown=abc:abc /opt/root/ /\n"
"COPY --from=build_edge --chown=abc:abc /opt/openems-edge.jar /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
"RUN find /etc/s6-overlay/ -type f -name 'run' -exec chmod +x {} \\;\n"
"ENV EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=\"-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError\"\n"
"VOLUME /var/opt/openems/config\n"
"VOLUME /var/opt/openems/data\n"
"EXPOSE 8080 8085\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**The base is the linuxserver.io Alpine image** with the tag `+edge+` "
"(Alpine development branch). It provides the init system s6-overlay, the "
"user `+abc+` and the helper `+lsiown+`. Because `+edge+` is a moving tag, "
"two builds of the same commit can contain different base packages."
msgstr ""
"**Basis ist das Alpine-Image von linuxserver.io** im Tag `+edge+` (Alpine-"
"Entwicklungszweig). Es bringt das Init-System s6-overlay, den Benutzer "
"`+abc+` und das Hilfsprogramm `+lsiown+` mit. Weil `+edge+` ein beweglicher "
"Tag ist, können zwei Builds desselben Commits unterschiedliche Basis-Pakete "
"enthalten."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Java** comes as a Temurin JRE from the Adoptium APK repository, version "
"from `+JAVA_VERSION+` (default 25, matching `+javac.target: 25+` in `+cnf/"
"build.bnd+`)."
msgstr ""
"**Java** kommt als Temurin-JRE aus dem APK-Repository von Adoptium, Version "
"aus `+JAVA_VERSION+` (Voreinstellung 25, passend zu `+javac.target: 25+` in "
"`+cnf/build.bnd+`). Im APK-Repository von Adoptium gibt es JRE-Pakete "
"`+temurin-NN-jre+` für die Versionen 8, 11, 17 und 20 bis 27 (Stand "
"01.11.2026, x86_64), also auch für 25."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"There is **no `+HEALTHCHECK+`** in the Dockerfiles. `+docker ps+` therefore "
"only shows “Up”, not “healthy”."
msgstr ""
"Es gibt **keinen `+HEALTHCHECK+`** in den Dockerfiles. `+docker ps+` zeigt "
"daher nur „Up“, nicht „healthy“."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start sequence (s6-overlay)"
msgstr "Startablauf (s6-overlay)"

#. type: #sec-start-sequence-s6-overlay
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The entry point is `+/init+` of s6-overlay. The services are under `+/etc/s6-"
"overlay/s6-rc.d/+` in the respective `+root/+` directory."
msgstr ""
"Der Einstiegspunkt ist `+/init+` von s6-overlay. Die Dienste liegen unter `+/"
"etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/+` im jeweiligen `+root/+`-Verzeichnis."

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Service\n"
"| Type\n"
"| Task\n"
"\n"
"| `+init-adduser+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| Sets UID/GID of the user `+abc+` from `+PUID+`/`+PGID+` (default 911/911), shows the banner.\n"
"| `+init-openems-config+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| If `+/var/opt/openems/config+` is empty, the default configuration is copied from `+/var/lib/openems-default-config/+` (Backend additionally `+metadata.json+`, see below).\n"
"| `+init-permissions+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| `+lsiown -R abc:abc /opt/openems /var/opt/openems+`\n"
"| `+svc-openems-edge+` (or `+-backend+`, `+-backend-edge+`)\n"
"| longrun\n"
"| Starts Java as user `+abc+`.\n"
msgstr ""
"| Dienst\n"
"| Typ\n"
"| Aufgabe\n"
"\n"
"| `+init-adduser+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| Setzt UID/GID des Benutzers `+abc+` aus `+PUID+`/`+PGID+` (Voreinstellung 911/911), zeigt das Banner.\n"
"| `+init-openems-config+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| Ist `+/var/opt/openems/config+` leer, wird die Grundkonfiguration aus `+/var/lib/openems-default-config/+` hineinkopiert (Backend zusätzlich `+metadata.json+`, siehe unten).\n"
"| `+init-permissions+`\n"
"| oneshot\n"
"| `+lsiown -R abc:abc /opt/openems /var/opt/openems+`\n"
"| `+svc-openems-edge+` (bzw. `+-backend+`, `+-backend-edge+`)\n"
"| longrun\n"
"| Startet Java als Benutzer `+abc+`.\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Java call of the Edge"
msgstr "Java-Aufruf der Edge"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"/usr/bin/java \\\n"
"  -Dosgi.clean=true \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.eventadmin.Timeout=0 \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.http.host=0.0.0.0 \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.http.port=8080 \\\n"
"  -Dfelix.cm.dir=/var/opt/openems/config \\\n"
"  -Dopenems.data.dir=/var/opt/openems/data \\\n"
"  -Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true \\\n"
"  $EXTRA_JVM_OPTS \\\n"
"  -jar /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
msgstr ""
"/usr/bin/java \\\n"
"  -Dosgi.clean=true \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.eventadmin.Timeout=0 \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.http.host=0.0.0.0 \\\n"
"  -Dorg.apache.felix.http.port=8080 \\\n"
"  -Dfelix.cm.dir=/var/opt/openems/config \\\n"
"  -Dopenems.data.dir=/var/opt/openems/data \\\n"
"  -Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true \\\n"
"  $EXTRA_JVM_OPTS \\\n"
"  -jar /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+felix.cm.dir+` and `+openems.data.dir+` override the paths `+c:/openems/…"
"+` from `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."
msgstr ""
"`+felix.cm.dir+` und `+openems.data.dir+` überschreiben die Pfade `+c:/"
"openems/…+` aus `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+org.apache.felix.http.host=0.0.0.0+`: the Apache Felix Web Console listens "
"on all interfaces of the container. If port 8080 is published, the console "
"is reachable from outside."
msgstr ""
"`+org.apache.felix.http.host=0.0.0.0+`: Die Apache Felix Web Console lauscht "
"auf allen Schnittstellen des Containers. Wird Port 8080 veröffentlicht, ist "
"die Konsole von außen erreichbar."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`pass:c[-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError]` is part of the default value of "
"`+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`: if memory runs out, the JVM exits and s6 restarts the "
"service. **If you set `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+` yourself, the default value is "
"replaced**; include this option if you want to keep it."
msgstr ""
"`pass:c[-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError]` steckt in der Voreinstellung von "
"`+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`: Bei Speichermangel beendet sich die JVM, s6 startet den "
"Dienst neu. **Wer `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+` selbst setzt, ersetzt die "
"Voreinstellung**; die Option also mit angeben, wenn sie bleiben soll."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Backend and Backend-Edge additionally have `pass:c[-XX:+UseZGC -XX:"
"+UseCompactObjectHeaders]` in the default value."
msgstr ""
"Backend und Backend-Edge haben in der Voreinstellung zusätzlich `pass:c[-XX:"
"+UseZGC -XX:+UseCompactObjectHeaders]`."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Readiness check:** `+s6-notifyoncheck -d -n 300 -w 1000 -c \"nc -z "
"127.0.0.1 8080\"+` reports the service as ready as soon as the Felix port "
"responds (up to 300 attempts at intervals of 1 s). This only takes effect "
"within s6, not as a Docker health check."
msgstr ""
"**Bereitschaftsprüfung:** `+s6-notifyoncheck -d -n 300 -w 1000 -c \"nc -z "
"127.0.0.1 8080\"+` meldet den Dienst als bereit, sobald der Felix-Port "
"antwortet (bis zu 300 Versuche im Abstand von 1 s). Das wirkt nur innerhalb "
"von s6, nicht als Docker-Healthcheck."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default configuration of the Edge"
msgstr "Grundkonfiguration der Edge"

#. type: #sec-default-configuration-of-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"At the first start, these files are copied to `+/var/opt/openems/config+`:"
msgstr ""
"Beim ersten Start werden diese Dateien nach `+/var/opt/openems/config+` "
"kopiert:"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| File\n"
"| Component\n"
"\n"
"| `+Core/*.config+`\n"
"| `+_appManager+`, `+_componentManager+`, `+_cycle+`, `+_energy+`, `+_meta+`, `+_predictorManager+`, `+_serialNumber+`, `+_sum+`\n"
"| `+Scheduler/AllAlphabetically/default.config+`\n"
"| `+scheduler0+` (all Controllers alphabetically)\n"
"| `+Controller/Api/Websocket/default.config+`\n"
"| `+ctrlApiWebsocket0+`, port 8085, `+apiTimeout+` 60 s\n"
msgstr ""
"| Datei\n"
"| Komponente\n"
"\n"
"| `+Core/*.config+`\n"
"| `+_appManager+`, `+_componentManager+`, `+_cycle+`, `+_energy+`, `+_meta+`, `+_predictorManager+`, `+_serialNumber+`, `+_sum+`\n"
"| `+Scheduler/AllAlphabetically/default.config+`\n"
"| `+scheduler0+` (alle Controller alphabetisch)\n"
"| `+Controller/Api/Websocket/default.config+`\n"
"| `+ctrlApiWebsocket0+`, Port 8085, `+apiTimeout+` 60 s\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"No devices, no Backend connection, no REST API, no Timedata (rrd4j). The "
"check “directory empty?” only applies at the very first start. If you want "
"to provide your own default configuration, put it in `+tools/docker/edge/"
"root/var/lib/openems-default-config/+` and rebuild the image, or fill the "
"volume before the first start."
msgstr ""
"Keine Geräte, kein Backend-Anschluss, keine REST-API, keine Timedata "
"(rrd4j). Die Prüfung „Verzeichnis leer?“ greift nur beim allerersten Start. "
"Wer eine eigene Grundkonfiguration mitliefern will, legt sie in `+tools/"
"docker/edge/root/var/lib/openems-default-config/+` ab und baut das Image "
"neu, oder befüllt das Volume vor dem ersten Start."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variables (Java images)"
msgstr "Umgebungsvariablen (Java-Images)"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variable\n"
"| Default\n"
"| Effect\n"
"\n"
"| `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`\n"
"| see above\n"
"| Additional JVM options, e.g. `+-Xmx512m+`, `+-Duser.timezone=Europe/Berlin+` or `+-agentlib:jdwp=…+` for debugging.\n"
"| `+PUID+` / `+PGID+`\n"
"| 911 / 911\n"
"| UID/GID of the user `+abc+`. Important for bind mounts instead of named volumes and for access to devices such as `+/dev/ttyUSB0+`.\n"
"| `+TZ+`\n"
"| –\n"
"| Time zone of the JVM. On Linux, Java adopts the variable `+TZ+`; the time zone data (`+tzdata+`) is installed by the linuxserver base image. Not set in the OpenEMS code.\n"
msgstr ""
"| Variable\n"
"| Voreinstellung\n"
"| Wirkung\n"
"\n"
"| `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`\n"
"| siehe oben\n"
"| Zusätzliche JVM-Optionen, z. B. `+-Xmx512m+`, `+-Duser.timezone=Europe/Berlin+` oder `+-agentlib:jdwp=…+` zum Debuggen.\n"
"| `+PUID+` / `+PGID+`\n"
"| 911 / 911\n"
"| UID/GID des Benutzers `+abc+`. Wichtig bei Bind-Mounts statt Named Volumes und für den Zugriff auf Geräte wie `+/dev/ttyUSB0+`.\n"
"| `+TZ+`\n"
"| –\n"
"| Zeitzone der JVM. Java übernimmt unter Linux die Variable `+TZ+`, die Zeitzonendaten (`+tzdata+`) installiert das linuxserver-Basisimage. Im OpenEMS-Code nicht gesetzt.\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operating the Edge with the UI"
msgstr "Edge mit UI betreiben"

#. type: #sec-operating-the-edge-with-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Compose file is in xref:edge/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy OpenEMS Edge to "
"Docker] and in `+tools/docker/edge/docker-compose.yml+`. How to log in is "
"described there and in xref:gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]."
msgstr ""
"Die Compose-Datei steht in xref:latest@edge/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy "
"OpenEMS Edge to Docker] und in `+tools/docker/edge/docker-compose.yml+`. Die "
"Anmeldung beschreiben diese Seite und "
"xref:latest@gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]."

#. type: #sec-operating-the-edge-with-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Port 8085 does not need to be published** if only the UI from the "
"container is used: the UI connects to `+ws(s)://<site>/openems-edge+` (`+ui/"
"src/themes/openems/environments/edge-docker.ts+`), and nginx forwards this "
"to the Edge in the Compose network. Publishing is only needed for direct "
"clients (e.g. `+ng serve+` on the development machine or scripts)."
msgstr ""
"**Port 8085 muss nicht veröffentlicht werden**, wenn nur die UI aus dem "
"Container genutzt wird: Die UI baut ihre Verbindung zu `+ws(s)://<Seite>/"
"openems-edge+` auf (`+ui/src/themes/openems/environments/edge-docker.ts+`), "
"und nginx leitet sie im Compose-Netz an die Edge weiter. Die "
"Veröffentlichung braucht man nur für direkte Clients (z. B. `+ng serve+` auf "
"dem Entwicklungsrechner oder Skripte)."

#. type: #sec-operating-the-edge-with-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Apache Felix Web Console is also no longer needed after setup. In "
"operation, port 8080 should not be open to the network or should only be "
"bound to `+127.0.0.1+` (`+127.0.0.1:8080:8080+`)."
msgstr ""
"Ebenso ist die Apache Felix Web Console nach der Einrichtung nicht mehr "
"nötig. Im Betrieb sollte Port 8080 nicht offen ins Netz zeigen oder nur an "
"`+127.0.0.1+` gebunden werden (`+127.0.0.1:8080:8080+`)."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data and configuration"
msgstr "Daten und Konfiguration"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Volume\n"
"| Path in the container\n"
"| Content\n"
"\n"
"| `+openems-edge-conf+`\n"
"| `+/var/opt/openems/config+`\n"
"| Configuration Admin files (`+*.config+`), one file per component\n"
"| `+openems-edge-data+`\n"
"| `+/var/opt/openems/data+`\n"
"| Data of the components, e.g. rrd4j history\n"
msgstr ""
"| Volume\n"
"| Pfad im Container\n"
"| Inhalt\n"
"\n"
"| `+openems-edge-conf+`\n"
"| `+/var/opt/openems/config+`\n"
"| Configuration-Admin-Dateien (`+*.config+`), eine Datei je Komponente\n"
"| `+openems-edge-data+`\n"
"| `+/var/opt/openems/data+`\n"
"| Daten der Komponenten, z. B. rrd4j-Historie, Zustände\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "Backup:"
msgstr "Sichern:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker run --rm -v openems-edge-conf:/src:ro -v \"$PWD\":/dst alpine \\\n"
"  tar czf /dst/openems-edge-conf.tgz -C /src .\n"
msgstr ""
"docker run --rm -v openems-edge-conf:/src:ro -v \"$PWD\":/dst alpine \\\n"
"  tar czf /dst/openems-edge-conf.tgz -C /src .\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Note: Compose prefixes volume names with the project name (usually the "
"directory name, e.g. `+edge_openems-edge-conf+`). `+docker volume ls+` shows "
"the real name."
msgstr ""
"Hinweis: Compose stellt Volume-Namen den Projektnamen voran (meist der "
"Verzeichnisname, z. B. `+edge_openems-edge-conf+`). Den echten Namen zeigt "
"`+docker volume ls+`."

#. type: Title ====
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paths on the Docker host"
msgstr "Pfade auf dem Docker-Host"

#. type: #sec-paths-on-the-docker-host
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"On a normal Docker installation (Ubuntu, Debian), named volumes are located "
"under `+/var/lib/docker/volumes/<project>_<volume>/_data+`. This does not "
"apply if Docker is installed as a Snap (then `+/var/snap/docker/common/var-"
"lib-docker/volumes/…+`), runs in rootless mode or has its own `+data-root+`. "
"The actual path is shown by:"
msgstr ""
"Bei einer normalen Docker-Installation (Ubuntu, Debian) liegen benannte "
"Volumes unter `+/var/lib/docker/volumes/<Projekt>_<Volume>/_data+`. Das gilt "
"nicht, wenn Docker als Snap installiert ist (dann `+/var/snap/docker/common/"
"var-lib-docker/volumes/…+`), im Rootless-Modus läuft oder ein eigenes `+data-"
"root+` gesetzt ist. Den tatsächlichen Pfad zeigt:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker volume inspect <project>_openems-edge-conf --format '{{.Name}}: {{.Mountpoint}}'\n"
msgstr "docker volume inspect <Projekt>_openems-edge-conf --format '{{.Name}}: {{.Mountpoint}}'\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Root permissions are required for `+/var/lib/docker+`. The files belong to "
"the user `+abc+` in the container (UID 911)."
msgstr ""
"Für `+/var/lib/docker+` sind root-Rechte nötig. Die Dateien gehören dem "
"Benutzer `+abc+` im Container (UID 911)."

#. type: Title ====
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accessing files"
msgstr "Zugriff auf Dateien"

#. type: #sec-accessing-files
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"In the Compose file of the repository, the container is called "
"`+openems_edge+`; `+docker ps+` shows the real name."
msgstr ""
"In der Compose-Datei des Repositorys heißt der Container `+openems_edge+`; "
"den echten Namen zeigt `+docker ps+`."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker exec -it openems_edge bash                    # as root\n"
"docker exec -it -u abc openems_edge bash             # as the user of the Edge\n"
"docker exec -u abc openems_edge ls -R /var/opt/openems/config\n"
"docker cp openems_edge:/var/opt/openems/config ./config-copy\n"
msgstr ""
"docker exec -it openems_edge bash                    # als root\n"
"docker exec -it -u abc openems_edge bash             # als Benutzer der Edge\n"
"docker exec -u abc openems_edge ls -R /var/opt/openems/config\n"
"docker cp openems_edge:/var/opt/openems/config ./config-kopie\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Only edit `+.config+` files directly when the container is stopped (`+docker "
"compose stop openems-edge+`) and do not change owner and permissions. "
"Reason: Felix Configuration Admin (version 1.9.26) keeps the configurations "
"in memory (`+CachingPersistenceManagerProxy+`) and does not re-read the "
"files during operation. A change to the file therefore only takes effect "
"after a restart. If the same configuration is saved beforehand via the UI, "
"Configuration Admin writes the state from memory to the file, and the manual "
"change is gone. During operation, it is better to make changes via the UI or "
"the Apache Felix Web Console."
msgstr ""
"`+.config+`-Dateien direkt nur bei gestopptem Container bearbeiten (`+docker "
"compose stop openems-edge+`) und Eigentümer und Rechte nicht ändern. Grund: "
"Felix Configuration Admin (Version 1.9.26) hält die Konfigurationen im "
"Speicher (`+CachingPersistenceManagerProxy+`) und liest die Dateien im "
"laufenden Betrieb nicht neu. Eine Änderung an der Datei wirkt deshalb erst "
"nach einem Neustart. Wird dieselbe Konfiguration vorher über die UI "
"gespeichert, schreibt Configuration Admin den Stand aus dem Speicher in die "
"Datei, und die Handänderung ist weg. Im laufenden Betrieb besser über die UI "
"oder die Apache Felix Web Console ändern."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restarting"
msgstr "Neu starten"

#. type: #sec-restarting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "In the directory of the Compose file:"
msgstr "Im Verzeichnis der Compose-Datei:"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Command\n"
"| Effect\n"
"| When\n"
"\n"
"| `+docker compose restart <service>+`\n"
"| restarts the existing container with its previous settings\n"
"| restart the Edge, e.g. after changing `+.config+` files\n"
"| `+docker compose up -d <service>+`\n"
"| recreates the container if the Compose file has changed\n"
"| after changing `+hostname+`, `+environment+` (e.g. `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`), ports, mounts or image\n"
"| `+docker compose up -d --force-recreate <service>+`\n"
"| always recreates the container\n"
"| if only the content of a bind mount has changed and you want to be sure\n"
msgstr ""
"| Befehl\n"
"| Wirkung\n"
"| Wann\n"
"\n"
"| `+docker compose restart <dienst>+`\n"
"| Startet den bestehenden Container mit seinen bisherigen Einstellungen neu\n"
"| Edge neu starten, z. B. nach Änderung von `+.config+`-Dateien\n"
"| `+docker compose up -d <dienst>+`\n"
"| Erstellt den Container neu, wenn sich die Compose-Datei geändert hat\n"
"| Nach Änderung von `+hostname+`, `+environment+` (z. B. `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+`), Ports, Mounts oder Image\n"
"| `+docker compose up -d --force-recreate <dienst>+`\n"
"| Erstellt den Container in jedem Fall neu\n"
"| Wenn sich nur der Inhalt eines Bind-Mounts geändert hat und man sichergehen will\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The volumes are retained in all three cases. There is no `+systemctl restart "
"openems+` in the container as on a Debian installation; the Edge is started "
"and monitored by s6."
msgstr ""
"Die Volumes bleiben in allen drei Fällen erhalten. Ein `+systemctl restart "
"openems+` wie auf einer Debian-Installation gibt es im Container nicht; die "
"Edge wird von s6 gestartet und überwacht."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Restarting only the Java process, without the container (derived from the "
"structure of s6-overlay v3, not checked in the container):"
msgstr ""
"Nur den Java-Prozess neu starten, ohne den Container (abgeleitet aus dem "
"Aufbau von s6-overlay v3, nicht im Container geprüft):"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker exec openems_edge ls /run/service                     # check the path\n"
"docker exec openems_edge s6-svc -r /run/service/svc-openems-edge\n"
msgstr ""
"docker exec openems_edge ls /run/service                     # Pfad prüfen\n"
"docker exec openems_edge s6-svc -r /run/service/svc-openems-edge\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update"
msgstr "Update"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker compose pull\n"
"docker compose up -d\n"
msgstr ""
"docker compose pull\n"
"docker compose up -d\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Configuration and data are retained in the volumes. `+Core.Host+` recognizes "
"the container by the file `+/.dockerenv+` and then uses "
"`+OperatingSystemDocker+`. Network settings, network information, system "
"restart and system update are not implemented there; the UI receives an "
"error message or does not offer an update. Updates in Docker operation are "
"done via new images."
msgstr ""
"Konfiguration und Daten bleiben in den Volumes erhalten. `+Core.Host+` "
"erkennt den Container an der Datei `+/.dockerenv+` und nutzt dann "
"`+OperatingSystemDocker+`. Netzwerk-Einstellungen, Netzwerk-Infos, Neustart "
"des Systems und System-Update sind dort nicht umgesetzt; die UI bekommt eine "
"Fehlermeldung bzw. bietet kein Update an. Updates laufen im Docker-Betrieb "
"über neue Images."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building images yourself"
msgstr "Images selbst bauen"

#. type: #sec-building-images-yourself
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "In the root directory of the repository:"
msgstr "Im Wurzelverzeichnis des Repositorys:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker build . -t openems_edge         -f tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_ui-edge      -f tools/docker/ui/Dockerfile.edge\n"
"docker build . -t openems_backend      -f tools/docker/backend/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_backend-edge -f tools/docker/backend-edge/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_ui-backend   -f tools/docker/ui/Dockerfile.backend\n"
msgstr ""
"docker build . -t openems_edge         -f tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_ui-edge      -f tools/docker/ui/Dockerfile.edge\n"
"docker build . -t openems_backend      -f tools/docker/backend/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_backend-edge -f tools/docker/backend-edge/Dockerfile\n"
"docker build . -t openems_ui-backend   -f tools/docker/ui/Dockerfile.backend\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Then enter `+image: openems_edge+` etc. in the Compose file, or have Compose "
"build it directly:"
msgstr ""
"In der Compose-Datei dann `+image: openems_edge+` usw. eintragen, oder in "
"Compose direkt bauen lassen:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  openems-edge:\n"
"    build:\n"
"      context: /path/to/openems\n"
"      dockerfile: tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile\n"
"    image: openems_edge:dev\n"
msgstr ""
"  openems-edge:\n"
"    build:\n"
"      context: /pfad/zum/openems\n"
"      dockerfile: tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile\n"
"    image: openems_edge:dev\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Close Eclipse** or at least stop the automatic build. If another program "
"accesses the project files during the build, according to the README the "
"build aborts with “failed to solve: error from sender: context canceled”."
msgstr ""
"**Eclipse schließen** oder zumindest den automatischen Build anhalten. "
"Greift ein anderes Programm während des Builds auf die Projektdateien zu, "
"bricht der Build laut README mit „failed to solve: error from sender: "
"context canceled“ ab."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The build context comprises the entire repository, and there is no "
"`+.dockerignore+`. `+ui/node_modules+`, `+build/+`, `+generated/+` and "
"`+.metadata+` (Eclipse) are therefore also transferred. This makes the build "
"slower (not measured)."
msgstr ""
"Der Build-Kontext umfasst das ganze Repository. Eine `+.dockerignore+` gibt "
"es nicht, deshalb werden auch `+ui/node_modules+`, `+build/+`, `+generated/"
"+` und `+.metadata+` (Eclipse) übertragen. Das macht den Build langsam, "
"schadet aber nicht (nicht gemessen)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**For a different architecture** (e.g. arm64 for a Raspberry Pi, built on an "
"amd64 machine) with buildx (not tried out):"
msgstr ""
"**Für eine andere Architektur** (z. B. arm64 für einen Raspberry Pi, auf "
"einem amd64-Rechner gebaut) mit buildx (nicht ausprobiert):"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker buildx build --platform linux/arm64 -t openems_edge:arm64 \\\n"
"  -f tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile --load .\n"
msgstr ""
"docker buildx build --platform linux/arm64 -t openems_edge:arm64 \\\n"
"  -f tools/docker/edge/Dockerfile --load .\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI image"
msgstr "UI-Image"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ARG NODE=24\n"
"ARG NPM=11\n"
"ARG VERSION=\"openems,openems-edge-docker,prod\"\n"
msgstr ""
"ARG NODE=24\n"
"ARG NPM=11\n"
"ARG VERSION=\"openems,openems-edge-docker,prod\"\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM node:${NODE}-alpine AS build_ui\n"
"COPY ui/ /src/\n"
"...\n"
"RUN npm install -g \"npm@${NPM}\" && npm ci && node_modules/.bin/ng build -c \"$VERSION\"\n"
msgstr ""
"FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM node:${NODE}-alpine AS build_ui\n"
"COPY ui/ /src/\n"
"...\n"
"RUN npm install -g \"npm@${NPM}\" && npm ci && node_modules/.bin/ng build -c \"$VERSION\"\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FROM ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:edge AS ui_base\n"
"RUN apk add --update --no-cache nginx openssl bash dos2unix rsync gettext\n"
"...\n"
"COPY --from=build_ui --chown=abc:abc /src/target/ /var/www/html/openems/\n"
msgstr ""
"FROM ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:edge AS ui_base\n"
"RUN apk add --update --no-cache nginx openssl bash dos2unix rsync gettext\n"
"...\n"
"COPY --from=build_ui --chown=abc:abc /src/target/ /var/www/html/openems/\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+VERSION+` selects the Angular configuration from `+ui/angular.json+`: "
"theme (`+openems+`), environment (`+openems-edge-docker+` or `+openems-"
"backend-docker+`) and `+prod+`. A separate theme can be built with `+--build-"
"arg VERSION=…+` if it is entered in `+angular.json+`."
msgstr ""
"`+VERSION+` wählt die Angular-Konfiguration aus `+ui/angular.json+`: Theme "
"(`+openems+`), Umgebung (`+openems-edge-docker+` bzw. `+openems-backend-"
"docker+`) und `+prod+`. Ein eigenes Theme lässt sich so mit `+--build-arg "
"VERSION=…+` bauen, wenn es in `+angular.json+` eingetragen ist."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Unlike the Java images, `+ui/+` is copied into the image here via `+COPY+`. "
"`+npm ci+` deletes an existing `+node_modules+` and reinstalls; a local "
"`+node_modules+` only increases the build context."
msgstr ""
"Anders als bei den Java-Images wird `+ui/+` hier per `+COPY+` in das Image "
"kopiert. Ein lokales `+ui/node_modules+` landet damit ebenfalls im Build-"
"Kontext und in der Build-Stufe; `+npm ci+` löscht ein vorhandenes "
"`+node_modules+` und installiert neu."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing the program and the UI"
msgstr "Programm und Oberfläche austauschen"

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-program-and-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"This section describes how to replace the program (JAR) and the UI in a "
"running Docker installation without building an image, and how to test an "
"Edge beforehand as a clone. Check the names of containers and volumes "
"beforehand with `+docker compose ps+` and `+docker volume ls+`."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Abschnitt beschreibt, wie man in einer laufenden Docker-Installation "
"das Programm (JAR) und die Oberfläche austauscht, ohne ein Image zu bauen, "
"und wie man eine Edge vorher als Klon testet. Namen von Containern und "
"Volumes vorher mit `+docker compose ps+` und `+docker volume ls+` prüfen."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing the program (JAR)"
msgstr "Programm (JAR) austauschen"

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-program-jar
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The start command in the container always calls `+/opt/openems/openems-"
"edge.jar+`, with `+-Dosgi.clean=true+`. The bundle cache is therefore "
"emptied at every start, so a new JAR takes full effect."
msgstr ""
"Der Startbefehl im Container ruft immer `+/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar+` "
"auf, mit `+-Dosgi.clean=true+`. Der Bundle-Zwischenspeicher wird also bei "
"jedem Start geleert, ein neues JAR wirkt vollständig."

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-program-jar
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "**New official image:** see <<sec-update,Update>>."
msgstr "**Neues offizielles Image:** siehe <<sec-update,Update>>."

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-program-jar
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Your own JAR:** build it in the repository and place it over the JAR in "
"the image."
msgstr "**Eigenes JAR:** im Repository bauen und über das JAR im Image legen."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./gradlew buildEdge                      # creates build/openems-edge.jar\n"
"sha256sum build/openems-edge.jar\n"
"# copy it to the Docker host, then in the Compose file:\n"
"#   volumes:\n"
"#     - ./openems-edge.jar:/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar:ro\n"
"docker compose up -d --force-recreate openems-edge\n"
"docker exec openems_edge sha256sum /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
msgstr ""
"./gradlew buildEdge                      # erzeugt build/openems-edge.jar\n"
"sha256sum build/openems-edge.jar\n"
"# auf den Docker-Host kopieren, dann in der Compose-Datei:\n"
"#   volumes:\n"
"#     - ./openems-edge.jar:/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar:ro\n"
"docker compose up -d --force-recreate openems-edge\n"
"docker exec openems_edge sha256sum /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The state of the working directory is built, including changes that have not "
"been checked in, e.g. to `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."
msgstr ""
"Gebaut wird der Stand des Arbeitsverzeichnisses, also auch nicht "
"eingecheckte Änderungen, z. B. an `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."

#. type: Title ====
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing it directly by copying"
msgstr "Direkt durch Kopieren ersetzen"

#. type: #sec-replacing-it-directly-by-copying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Without changing the Compose file and without recreating the container, the "
"JAR can also be overwritten directly. The container is stopped for this so "
"that the running JVM does not read the JAR while it is being overwritten "
"(not tried out)."
msgstr ""
"Ohne Änderung der Compose-Datei und ohne Neuerstellen des Containers lässt "
"sich das JAR auch direkt überschreiben. Der Container wird dafür angehalten, "
"damit die laufende JVM das JAR nicht liest, während es überschrieben wird "
"(nicht ausprobiert)."

#. type: #sec-replacing-it-directly-by-copying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**JAR bound via bind mount:** overwrite the file on the host. `+cp+` on an "
"existing file writes to the same file; the bind mount then points to the new "
"content without recreating. With `+:ro+`, only access from the container is "
"blocked."
msgstr ""
"**JAR per Bind-Mount eingebunden:** die Datei auf dem Host überschreiben. "
"`+cp+` auf eine bestehende Datei schreibt in dieselbe Datei; der Bind-Mount "
"zeigt danach ohne Neuerstellen auf den neuen Inhalt. Mit `+:ro+` ist nur der "
"Zugriff aus dem Container gesperrt."

#. type: #sec-replacing-it-directly-by-copying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**JAR in the image, without bind mount:** copy it into the container with "
"`+docker cp+`."
msgstr ""
"**JAR im Image, ohne Bind-Mount:** mit `+docker cp+` in den Container "
"kopieren."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker stop openems_edge\n"
"docker cp build/openems-edge.jar openems_edge:/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
"docker start openems_edge\n"
"docker exec openems_edge sha256sum /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
msgstr ""
"docker stop openems_edge\n"
"docker cp build/openems-edge.jar openems_edge:/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"
"docker start openems_edge\n"
"docker exec openems_edge sha256sum /opt/openems/openems-edge.jar\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"A JAR copied with `+docker cp+` ends up in the writable layer of the "
"container. It is retained with `+docker stop+`/`+start+` and `+docker "
"restart+`, but is lost as soon as the container is recreated. For a "
"permanent replacement, use the bind mount."
msgstr ""
"Mit `+docker cp+` kopiert landet das JAR in der beschreibbaren Schicht des "
"Containers. Es bleibt bei `+docker stop+`/`+start+` und `+docker restart+` "
"erhalten, geht aber verloren, sobald der Container neu erstellt wird. Für "
"einen dauerhaften Austausch den Bind-Mount verwenden."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing the UI"
msgstr "Oberfläche austauschen"

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Official image:** `+docker compose pull openems-ui+` and `+docker compose "
"up -d openems-ui+`. Changed nginx templates do not reach an existing volume "
"`+/etc/nginx+` (see <<sec-ui-pitfalls,UI pitfalls>>)."
msgstr ""
"**Offizielles Image:** `+docker compose pull openems-ui+` und `+docker "
"compose up -d openems-ui+`. Geänderte nginx-Vorlagen erreichen ein "
"bestehendes Volume `+/etc/nginx+` nicht (siehe <<sec-ui-"
"pitfalls,Stolperstellen der UI>>)."

#. type: #sec-replacing-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Your own UI:** build it with the same Angular configuration as the "
"Dockerfile and place the result over the web directory of the container `+/"
"var/www/html/openems+`. The build result is in `+ui/target+`."
msgstr ""
"**Eigene Oberfläche:** mit derselben Angular-Konfiguration bauen wie das "
"Dockerfile und das Ergebnis über das Web-Verzeichnis des Containers `+/var/"
"www/html/openems+` legen. Das Build-Ergebnis liegt in `+ui/target+`."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cd ui\n"
"npm ci\n"
"node_modules/.bin/ng build -c \"openems,openems-edge-docker,prod\"\n"
"ls target/index.html\n"
"# copy the content of ui/target to the Docker host, then in the Compose file:\n"
"#   volumes:\n"
"#     - ./openems-www:/var/www/html/openems:ro\n"
"docker compose up -d --force-recreate openems-ui\n"
msgstr ""
"cd ui\n"
"npm ci\n"
"node_modules/.bin/ng build -c \"openems,openems-edge-docker,prod\"\n"
"ls target/index.html\n"
"# Inhalt von ui/target auf den Docker-Host kopieren, dann in der Compose-Datei:\n"
"#   volumes:\n"
"#     - ./openems-www:/var/www/html/openems:ro\n"
"docker compose up -d --force-recreate openems-ui\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Then reload the page in the browser without cache. These steps are derived "
"from the Dockerfile and Compose file and have not been tried out."
msgstr ""
"Danach die Seite im Browser ohne Cache neu laden. Die Schritte sind aus "
"Dockerfile und Compose-Datei abgeleitet und nicht ausprobiert."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Loading bundles via FileInstall"
msgstr "Bundles über FileInstall nachladen"

#. type: #sec-loading-bundles-via-fileinstall
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The bundle `+org.apache.felix.fileinstall+` is part of the Edge and monitors "
"a directory: it installs bundles (`+.jar+`) and configurations (`+.cfg+`, "
"`+.config+`) placed there during operation. The start script of the image "
"does not set `+felix.fileinstall.dir+`. Without this, FileInstall uses `+./"
"load+`, relative to the working directory of the JVM, i.e. the service "
"directory of s6. This is neither in a volume nor in a bind mount, so the "
"directory in the container should have its own location."
msgstr ""
"Das Bundle `+org.apache.felix.fileinstall+` ist Teil der Edge und überwacht "
"ein Verzeichnis: Dort abgelegte Bundles (`+.jar+`) und Konfigurationen "
"(`+.cfg+`, `+.config+`) installiert es im laufenden Betrieb. Das Startskript "
"des Images setzt `+felix.fileinstall.dir+` nicht. Ohne Angabe nimmt "
"FileInstall `+./load+`, relativ zum Arbeitsverzeichnis der JVM, also dem "
"Dienstverzeichnis von s6. Das liegt weder in einem Volume noch in einem Bind-"
"Mount, deshalb gehört das Verzeichnis im Container an einen eigenen Ort."

#. type: #sec-loading-bundles-via-fileinstall
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**1. Create the folder on the host,** in the Compose directory. The Edge "
"runs as `+abc+` in the container, and the files must be readable for this "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"**1. Ordner auf dem Host anlegen,** im Compose-Verzeichnis. Die Edge läuft "
"im Container als `+abc+`, die Dateien müssen für diesen Benutzer lesbar sein:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mkdir -p load\n"
"chmod a+rX load\n"
msgstr ""
"mkdir -p load\n"
"chmod a+rX load\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "**2. Change the Compose file,** for the Edge service:"
msgstr "**2. Compose-Datei ändern,** beim Dienst der Edge:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    environment:\n"
"      - EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError -Dfelix.fileinstall.dir=/opt/openems/load\n"
"    volumes:\n"
"      - ./load:/opt/openems/load:ro\n"
msgstr ""
"    environment:\n"
"      - EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError -Dfelix.fileinstall.dir=/opt/openems/load\n"
"    volumes:\n"
"      - ./load:/opt/openems/load:ro\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The start script splits the options at spaces, so the path must not contain "
"any."
msgstr ""
"Das Startskript trennt die Optionen an Leerzeichen, der Pfad darf also keine "
"enthalten."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**3. Recreate the container.** `+docker compose restart+` is not sufficient "
"because environment and mounts change. The volumes are retained."
msgstr ""
"**3. Container neu erstellen.** `+docker compose restart+` reicht nicht, "
"weil sich Umgebung und Mounts ändern. Die Volumes bleiben erhalten."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose up -d <service>\n"
msgstr "docker compose up -d <dienst>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**4. Check:** copy a bundle to the folder. It must appear as `+Active+` in "
"the Apache Felix Web Console under `+/system/console/bundles+`. FileInstall "
"checks the directory every 2 seconds (`+felix.fileinstall.poll+`, default "
"2000 ms)."
msgstr ""
"**4. Prüfen:** ein Bundle in den Ordner kopieren. Es muss in der Apache "
"Felix Web Console unter `+/system/console/bundles+` als `+Active+` "
"erscheinen. FileInstall prüft das Verzeichnis alle 2 Sekunden "
"(`+felix.fileinstall.poll+`, Standard 2000 ms)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**New at every start:** the image starts with `+-Dosgi.clean=true+`, so the "
"file must remain in the folder."
msgstr ""
"**Bei jedem Start neu:** Das Image startet mit `+-Dosgi.clean=true+`. Die "
"Datei muss also im Ordner liegen bleiben."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Bundle missing in the UI:** `+EdgeConfigWorker+` only reads the Factories "
"when rebuilding the `+EdgeConfig+`, i.e. on the first build and when a "
"configuration is deleted. It does not react to new bundles. A bundle loaded "
"later is then missing under “Install components”. Remedy: create a "
"configuration in the Apache Felix Web Console and delete it again."
msgstr ""
"**Bundle fehlt in der Oberfläche:** `+EdgeConfigWorker+` liest die Factories "
"nur beim Neuaufbau der `+EdgeConfig+`, also beim ersten Aufbau und wenn eine "
"Konfiguration gelöscht wird. Auf neue Bundles reagiert er nicht. Ein später "
"geladenes Bundle fehlt dann unter „Komponenten installieren“. Abhilfe: in "
"der Apache Felix Web Console eine Konfiguration anlegen und wieder löschen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Security:** anyone who can write to the folder can execute code in the "
"Edge. `+:ro+` only protects against write access from the container."
msgstr ""
"**Sicherheit:** Wer in den Ordner schreiben darf, kann Code in der Edge "
"ausführen. `+:ro+` schützt nur vor Schreibzugriffen aus dem Container."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cloning an Edge for testing"
msgstr "Edge zum Testen klonen"

#. type: #sec-cloning-an-edge-for-testing
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"A clone is a second container with copies of the configuration and data, its "
"own ports and its own name. The original continues to run unchanged. The "
"clone receives the same configuration and thus queries and controls the same "
"devices, in parallel with the original. It therefore first starts without a "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Ein Klon ist ein zweiter Container mit Kopien von Konfiguration und Daten, "
"eigenen Ports und eigenem Namen. Das Original läuft unverändert weiter. Der "
"Klon bekommt dieselbe Konfiguration und fragt damit dieselben Geräte ab bzw. "
"steuert sie, parallel zum Original. Deshalb startet er zuerst ohne Netz."

#. type: #sec-cloning-an-edge-for-testing
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "**1. Read out the structure of the original:**"
msgstr "**1. Aufbau des Originals auslesen:**"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker inspect openems_edge --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Type}} {{if eq .Type \"volume\"}}{{.Name}}{{else}}{{.Source}}{{end}} {{.Destination}}{{println}}{{end}}'\n"
"docker inspect openems_edge --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | grep -v -E '^(PATH|HOME|LANG|S6_|LSIO_|TERM|XDG_|VIRTUAL_ENV)'\n"
msgstr ""
"docker inspect openems_edge --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Type}} {{if eq .Type \"volume\"}}{{.Name}}{{else}}{{.Source}}{{end}} {{.Destination}}{{println}}{{end}}'\n"
"docker inspect openems_edge --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | grep -v -E '^(PATH|HOME|LANG|S6_|LSIO_|TERM|XDG_|VIRTUAL_ENV)'\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**2. Copy configuration and data.** Stop the original briefly so that the "
"data (rrd4j) is not written during copying. `+SRC_CONF+` and `+SRC_DATA+` "
"are the volume names from step 1:"
msgstr ""
"**2. Konfiguration und Daten kopieren.** Das Original dafür kurz anhalten, "
"damit die Daten (rrd4j) nicht während des Kopierens geschrieben werden. "
"`+SRC_CONF+` und `+SRC_DATA+` sind die Volume-Namen aus Schritt 1:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker stop openems_edge\n"
"docker volume create clone-conf\n"
"docker volume create clone-data\n"
"docker run --rm --network none -v \"$SRC_CONF\":/from:ro -v clone-conf:/to alpine cp -a /from/. /to/\n"
"docker run --rm --network none -v \"$SRC_DATA\":/from:ro -v clone-data:/to alpine cp -a /from/. /to/\n"
"docker start openems_edge\n"
msgstr ""
"docker stop openems_edge\n"
"docker volume create clone-conf\n"
"docker volume create clone-data\n"
"docker run --rm --network none -v \"$SRC_CONF\":/from:ro -v clone-conf:/to alpine cp -a /from/. /to/\n"
"docker run --rm --network none -v \"$SRC_DATA\":/from:ro -v clone-data:/to alpine cp -a /from/. /to/\n"
"docker start openems_edge\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "**3. Compose file of the clone, first start without a network:**"
msgstr "**3. Compose-Datei des Klons, erster Start ohne Netz:**"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"services:\n"
"  openems-edge-clone:\n"
"    image: openems/edge:latest\n"
"    container_name: openems-edge-clone\n"
"    hostname: openems-edge-clone\n"
"    restart: \"no\"\n"
"    network_mode: none\n"
"    volumes:\n"
"      - clone-conf:/var/opt/openems/config:rw\n"
"      - clone-data:/var/opt/openems/data:rw\n"
"volumes:\n"
"  clone-conf:\n"
"    external: true\n"
"  clone-data:\n"
"    external: true\n"
msgstr ""
"services:\n"
"  openems-edge-clone:\n"
"    image: openems/edge:latest\n"
"    container_name: openems-edge-clone\n"
"    hostname: openems-edge-clone\n"
"    restart: \"no\"\n"
"    network_mode: none\n"
"    volumes:\n"
"      - clone-conf:/var/opt/openems/config:rw\n"
"      - clone-data:/var/opt/openems/data:rw\n"
"volumes:\n"
"  clone-conf:\n"
"    external: true\n"
"  clone-data:\n"
"    external: true\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Errors from Bridges that cannot reach their device without a network are "
"expected here; `+UnsupportedClassVersionError+` and errors when starting "
"bundles must not occur."
msgstr ""
"Fehler von Bridges, die ohne Netz ihr Gerät nicht erreichen, sind hier "
"erwartet; `+UnsupportedClassVersionError+` und Fehler beim Start von Bundles "
"dürfen nicht vorkommen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**4. With network and UI.** Only when step 3 is clean and it is clear how "
"the clone may access devices: remove `+network_mode: none+`, bind ports only "
"to `+127.0.0.1+` and add `+openems/ui-edge+` with `+WEBSOCKET_HOST+` "
"pointing to the clone. Do not adopt the Modbus port of the original so that "
"Modbus clients do not accidentally connect to the clone."
msgstr ""
"**4. Mit Netz und Oberfläche.** Erst wenn Schritt 3 sauber ist und geklärt "
"ist, wie der Klon auf Geräte zugreifen darf: `+network_mode: none+` "
"entfernen, Ports nur an `+127.0.0.1+` binden und `+openems/ui-edge+` mit "
"`+WEBSOCKET_HOST+` auf den Klon ergänzen. Den Modbus-Port des Originals "
"nicht übernehmen, damit sich Modbus-Clients nicht versehentlich mit dem Klon "
"verbinden."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**5. Delete the clone.** First check what is being deleted; only names of "
"the clone may appear. `+docker volume rm+` permanently deletes the copies; "
"the volumes of the original remain untouched."
msgstr ""
"**5. Klon löschen.** Zuerst ansehen, was gelöscht wird; es dürfen nur Namen "
"des Klons erscheinen. `+docker volume rm+` löscht die Kopien endgültig; die "
"Volumes des Originals bleiben unberührt."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker ps -a --format '{{.Names}}' | grep clone\n"
"docker volume ls | grep clone\n"
"docker compose down\n"
"docker volume rm clone-conf clone-data\n"
msgstr ""
"docker ps -a --format '{{.Names}}' | grep clone\n"
"docker volume ls | grep clone\n"
"docker compose down\n"
"docker volume rm clone-conf clone-data\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"A clone built this way was tried out with a Java 25 image and a bound JAR; "
"deleting it was not."
msgstr ""
"Ein so aufgebauter Klon wurde mit einem Java-25-Image und einem "
"eingebundenen JAR ausprobiert; das Löschen nicht."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI container in detail"
msgstr "UI-Container im Detail"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr "Umgebungsvariablen"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variable\n"
"| Default\n"
"| Effect\n"
"\n"
"| `+WEBSOCKET_HOST+`\n"
"| `+<hostname>+` (placeholder)\n"
"| Target of the proxy for `+/openems-edge+` or `+/openems-backend+` and `+/rest+`. **If the placeholder remains, the container stops with `+sleep infinity+`** and reports this in the log.\n"
"| `+WEBSOCKET_PORT+`\n"
"| 8085 (Edge UI) or 8082 (Backend UI)\n"
"| port of the Websocket\n"
"| `+REST_PORT+`\n"
"| 8084\n"
"| port for `+/rest+`\n"
"| `+ENABLE_HTTPS+`\n"
"| false\n"
"| `+TEST+`/`+TESTING+`/`+SNAKEOIL+`: generate a self-signed certificate. `+PROD+`/`+PRODUCTION+`/`+TRUE+`/`+YES+`/`+1+`: own certificate expected. Otherwise HTTP only.\n"
"| `+UI_WEBSOCKET+`\n"
"| –\n"
"| Older format `+ws://host:port+`; only evaluated if `+WEBSOCKET_HOST+` still contains the placeholder.\n"
msgstr ""
"| Variable\n"
"| Voreinstellung\n"
"| Wirkung\n"
"\n"
"| `+WEBSOCKET_HOST+`\n"
"| `+<hostname>+` (Platzhalter)\n"
"| Ziel des Proxys für `+/openems-edge+` bzw. `+/openems-backend+` und `+/rest+`. **Bleibt der Platzhalter stehen, hält der Container mit `+sleep infinity+` an** und meldet das im Log.\n"
"| `+WEBSOCKET_PORT+`\n"
"| 8085 (Edge-UI) bzw. 8082 (Backend-UI)\n"
"| Port des Websockets\n"
"| `+REST_PORT+`\n"
"| 8084\n"
"| Port für `+/rest+`\n"
"| `+ENABLE_HTTPS+`\n"
"| false\n"
"| `+TEST+`/`+TESTING+`/`+SNAKEOIL+`: selbstsigniertes Zertifikat erzeugen. `+PROD+`/`+PRODUCTION+`/`+TRUE+`/`+YES+`/`+1+`: eigenes Zertifikat erwartet. Sonst nur HTTP.\n"
"| `+UI_WEBSOCKET+`\n"
"| –\n"
"| Älteres Format `+ws://host:port+`; wird nur ausgewertet, wenn `+WEBSOCKET_HOST+` noch den Platzhalter enthält.\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence at startup"
msgstr "Ablauf beim Start"

#. type: #sec-sequence-at-startup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+/defaults/nginx/+` is copied to `+/etc/nginx/+` with `+rsync --ignore-"
"existing+`."
msgstr ""
"`+/defaults/nginx/+` wird mit `+rsync --ignore-existing+` nach `+/etc/nginx/"
"+` kopiert."

#. type: #sec-sequence-at-startup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The finished `+.conf+` files are created from `+/etc/nginx/site-confs/80-"
"*.conf.tpl+` (and with HTTPS `+443-*.conf.tpl+`) via `+envsubst+`. Only `+"
"$WEBSOCKET_HOST+`, `+$WEBSOCKET_PORT+` and `+$REST_PORT+` are replaced. The "
"generated files are rewritten at every start."
msgstr ""
"Aus `+/etc/nginx/site-confs/80-*.conf.tpl+` (und bei HTTPS `+443-"
"*.conf.tpl+`) entstehen per `+envsubst+` die fertigen `+.conf+`-Dateien. "
"Ersetzt werden nur `+$WEBSOCKET_HOST+`, `+$WEBSOCKET_PORT+` und `+"
"$REST_PORT+`. Die erzeugten Dateien werden bei jedem Start neu geschrieben."

#. type: #sec-sequence-at-startup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "nginx starts in the foreground."
msgstr "nginx startet im Vordergrund."

#. type: #sec-sequence-at-startup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Proxy rules of the Edge UI (`+root-edge/defaults/nginx/site-confs/80-"
"openems.conf.tpl+`):"
msgstr ""
"Proxy-Regeln der Edge-UI (`+root-edge/defaults/nginx/site-confs/80-"
"openems.conf.tpl+`):"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"location / {\n"
"    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;\n"
"}\n"
"location /openems-edge {\n"
"    proxy_pass http://$WEBSOCKET_HOST:$WEBSOCKET_PORT;\n"
"    proxy_http_version 1.1;\n"
"    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n"
"    proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';\n"
"    ...\n"
"}\n"
"location /rest {\n"
"    proxy_pass http://$WEBSOCKET_HOST:$REST_PORT/rest;\n"
"    ...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"location / {\n"
"    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;\n"
"}\n"
"location /openems-edge {\n"
"    proxy_pass http://$WEBSOCKET_HOST:$WEBSOCKET_PORT;\n"
"    proxy_http_version 1.1;\n"
"    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n"
"    proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';\n"
"    ...\n"
"}\n"
"location /rest {\n"
"    proxy_pass http://$WEBSOCKET_HOST:$REST_PORT/rest;\n"
"    ...\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI pitfalls"
msgstr "Stolperstellen der UI"

#. type: #sec-ui-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+/etc/nginx+` is a volume.** Because of `+--ignore-existing+`, changed "
"templates from a newer image do not reach an existing volume. After an image "
"update with changed nginx files, delete the volume `+openems-ui-conf+` or "
"compare the files by hand. Conversely, your own changes to the `+.tpl+` "
"files are retained; changes to the generated `+.conf+` files are lost at the "
"next start."
msgstr ""
"**`+/etc/nginx+` ist ein Volume.** Wegen `+--ignore-existing+` erreichen "
"geänderte Vorlagen aus einem neueren Image ein bestehendes Volume nicht. "
"Nach einem Image-Update mit geänderten nginx-Dateien das Volume `+openems-ui-"
"conf+` löschen oder die Dateien von Hand abgleichen. Umgekehrt bleiben "
"eigene Änderungen an den `+.tpl+`-Dateien erhalten; Änderungen an den "
"erzeugten `+.conf+`-Dateien gehen beim nächsten Start verloren."

#. type: #sec-ui-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+/rest+` leads nowhere** as long as no REST/JSON API is set up on the "
"Edge on port 8084 (not in the default configuration)."
msgstr ""
"**`+/rest+` zeigt ins Leere**, solange auf der Edge keine REST/JSON-"
"Schnittstelle auf Port 8084 eingerichtet ist (nicht in der "
"Grundkonfiguration)."

#. type: #sec-ui-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**HTTPS with your own certificate:** put `+cert.crt+` and `+cert.key+` in `+/"
"etc/nginx/keys/+` (e.g. via bind mount). If they are missing with "
"`+ENABLE_HTTPS=PROD+`, the container stops with `+sleep infinity+`."
msgstr ""
"**HTTPS mit eigenem Zertifikat:** `+cert.crt+` und `+cert.key+` nach `+/etc/"
"nginx/keys/+` legen (z. B. per Bind-Mount). Fehlen sie bei "
"`+ENABLE_HTTPS=PROD+`, hält der Container mit `+sleep infinity+` an."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend with Backend-Edge, UI and InfluxDB"
msgstr "Backend mit Backend-Edge, UI und InfluxDB"

#. type: #sec-backend-with-backend-edge-ui-and-influxdb
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Compose files are in xref:backend/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy OpenEMS "
"Backend to Docker]."
msgstr ""
"Die Compose-Dateien stehen in xref:latest@backend/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy "
"OpenEMS Backend to Docker]."

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Edge (Controller Api Backend)\n"
"   |  ws:8081\n"
"   v\n"
"backend-edge (Backend.Edge.App)\n"
"   |  ws:8083\n"
"   v\n"
"backend (Edge.Manager, Ui.Websocket,      <--ws:8082--  ui-backend (nginx)\n"
"         Metadata.File, Timedata.*)                         ^\n"
"   |  http:8086                                             |  http:80\n"
"   v                                                     Browser\n"
"InfluxDB\n"
msgstr ""
"Edge (Controller Api Backend)\n"
"   |  ws:8081\n"
"   v\n"
"backend-edge (Backend.Edge.App)\n"
"   |  ws:8083\n"
"   v\n"
"backend (Edge.Manager, Ui.Websocket,      <--ws:8082--  ui-backend (nginx)\n"
"         Metadata.File, Timedata.*)                         ^\n"
"   |  http:8086                                             |  http:80\n"
"   v                                                     Browser\n"
"InfluxDB\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Edges do **not** connect to the container `+openems/backend+`, but to "
"`+openems/backend-edge+` on port 8081. The Compose file `+tools/docker/"
"backend/docker-compose.yml+` contains Backend, UI and InfluxDB, but **no** "
"Backend-Edge container; port 8083 is published there so that a separately "
"started Backend-Edge container can connect."
msgstr ""
"Die Edges verbinden sich **nicht** mit dem Container `+openems/backend+`, "
"sondern mit `+openems/backend-edge+` auf Port 8081. Die Compose-Datei in "
"`+tools/docker/backend/docker-compose.yml+` enthält Backend, UI und "
"InfluxDB, aber **keinen** Backend-Edge-Container; Port 8083 ist dort "
"veröffentlicht, damit ein separat gestarteter Backend-Edge-Container sich "
"verbinden kann."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting Backend-Edge to the Backend"
msgstr "Backend-Edge mit dem Backend verbinden"

#. type: #sec-connecting-backend-edge-to-the-backend
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The default configuration of Backend-Edge (`+Backend/Edge/App.config+`) "
"contains `+uri=\"ws://localhost:8083\"+`. In the container, `+localhost+` "
"points to the Backend-Edge container itself. After the first start, set the "
"field **Uri** of the “Backend Edge Application” to the Backend container in "
"the Apache Felix Web Console of Backend-Edge (`+http://<host>:8078/system/"
"console/configMgr+`):"
msgstr ""
"Die Grundkonfiguration von Backend-Edge (`+Backend/Edge/App.config+`) "
"enthält `+uri=\"ws://localhost:8083\"+`. Im Container zeigt `+localhost+` "
"auf den Backend-Edge-Container selbst. Nach dem ersten Start in der Apache "
"Felix Web Console von Backend-Edge (`+http://<host>:8078/system/console/"
"configMgr+`) bei „Backend Edge Application“ das Feld **Uri** auf den Backend-"
"Container setzen:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "ws://openems-backend:8083\n"
msgstr "ws://openems-backend:8083\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Do not use an underscore in the host name.** `+BackendEdgeServerApp+` "
"creates a `+java.net.URI+` from it. Tried out with Java 23:"
msgstr ""
"**Keinen Unterstrich im Hostnamen verwenden.** `+BackendEdgeServerApp+` "
"erzeugt daraus ein `+java.net.URI+`. Ausprobiert mit Java 23:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ws://openems_backend:8083  host=null             port=-1\n"
"ws://openems-backend:8083  host=openems-backend  port=8083\n"
msgstr ""
"ws://openems_backend:8083  host=null             port=-1\n"
"ws://openems-backend:8083  host=openems-backend  port=8083\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+java.net.URI+` does not recognize host names with an underscore as a host. "
"That the Websocket connection therefore fails is concluded from this and has "
"not been checked in the running system. Therefore choose service and "
"container names with a hyphen in the Compose file, as in `+tools/docker/"
"backend/docker-compose.yml+`."
msgstr ""
"`+java.net.URI+` erkennt Hostnamen mit Unterstrich nicht als Host. Dass die "
"Websocket-Verbindung damit scheitert, ist daraus geschlossen und nicht im "
"laufenden System geprüft. Deshalb in der Compose-Datei Dienst- und "
"Containernamen mit Bindestrich wählen, wie in `+tools/docker/backend/docker-"
"compose.yml+`."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default configuration of the Backend"
msgstr "Grundkonfiguration des Backends"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| File\n"
"| Content\n"
"\n"
"| `+Edge/Manager.config+`\n"
"| port 8083, pool 10\n"
"| `+Ui/Websocket.config+`\n"
"| port 8082, pool 10\n"
"| `+Metadata/File.config+`\n"
"| `+path=\"/var/opt/openems/metadata.json\"+`\n"
"| `+Timedata/Dummy.config+`\n"
"| `+timedata0+`, does not store anything\n"
msgstr ""
"| Datei\n"
"| Inhalt\n"
"\n"
"| `+Edge/Manager.config+`\n"
"| Port 8083, Pool 10\n"
"| `+Ui/Websocket.config+`\n"
"| Port 8082, Pool 10\n"
"| `+Metadata/File.config+`\n"
"| `+path=\"/var/opt/openems/metadata.json\"+`\n"
"| `+Timedata/Dummy.config+`\n"
"| `+timedata0+`, speichert nichts\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Metadata:** At the first start, `+/var/lib/openems-default-metadata/"
"metadata.json+` is copied to `+/var/opt/openems/metadata.json+`. It contains "
"two demo Edges (`+edge0+`, `+edge1+`) with example Apikeys and setup "
"passwords from the public repository. Replace these entries with your own "
"values before productive use."
msgstr ""
"**Metadaten:** Beim ersten Start wird `+/var/lib/openems-default-metadata/"
"metadata.json+` nach `+/var/opt/openems/metadata.json+` kopiert. Sie enthält "
"zwei Demo-Edges (`+edge0+`, `+edge1+`) mit Beispiel-Apikeys und Setup-"
"Passwörtern aus dem öffentlichen Repository. Diese Einträge vor dem "
"produktiven Einsatz durch eigene Werte ersetzen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"**Caution, according to the script not in the volume:** `+/var/opt/openems/"
"metadata.json+` is located next to the volumes `+…/config+` and `+…/data+`, "
"not in them. If the container is recreated (e.g. after `+docker compose "
"pull+`), the file is gone. Since the configuration volume is then no longer "
"empty, the init script does not copy it again. According to the code, "
"`+Metadata.File+` then cannot read the file, writes a warning to the log and "
"knows no Edge, so no Edge can log in (not tried out). Remedy: in "
"`+Metadata.File+`, set the path to `+/var/opt/openems/data/metadata.json+` "
"and copy the file there, or bind the file via bind mount:"
msgstr ""
"**Achtung, laut Skript nicht im Volume:** `+/var/opt/openems/metadata.json+` "
"liegt neben den Volumes `+…/config+` und `+…/data+`, nicht darin. Wird der "
"Container neu erstellt (z. B. nach `+docker compose pull+`), ist die Datei "
"weg. Da das Konfigurationsvolume dann nicht mehr leer ist, kopiert das Init-"
"Skript sie auch nicht neu. Laut Code kann `+Metadata.File+` die Datei dann "
"nicht lesen, schreibt eine Warnung ins Log und kennt keine Edge, sodass sich "
"keine Edge anmelden kann (nicht ausprobiert). Abhilfe: In `+Metadata.File+` "
"den Pfad auf `+/var/opt/openems/data/metadata.json+` stellen und die Datei "
"dorthin kopieren, oder die Datei per Bind-Mount einbinden:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    volumes:\n"
"      - ./metadata.json:/var/opt/openems/metadata.json:rw\n"
msgstr ""
"    volumes:\n"
"      - ./metadata.json:/var/opt/openems/metadata.json:rw\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting InfluxDB"
msgstr "InfluxDB anbinden"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker exec openems-influxdb influx setup \\\n"
"  --username openems \\\n"
"  --password <your-password> \\\n"
"  --org openems.io \\\n"
"  --bucket openems \\\n"
"  --force\n"
"docker exec openems-influxdb influx auth list\n"
msgstr ""
"docker exec openems-influxdb influx setup \\\n"
"  --username openems \\\n"
"  --password <eigenes-Passwort> \\\n"
"  --org openems.io \\\n"
"  --bucket openems \\\n"
"  --force\n"
"docker exec openems-influxdb influx auth list\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The command must match the actual container name; the Compose files use "
"`+openems-influxdb+` with a hyphen."
msgstr ""
"Der Befehl muss zum tatsächlichen Containernamen passen; die Compose-Dateien "
"verwenden `+openems-influxdb+` mit Bindestrich."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Use your own password. The password and token do not belong in the Compose "
"file in Git."
msgstr ""
"Ein eigenes Passwort verwenden. Passwort und Token gehören nicht in die "
"Compose-Datei im Git."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Then delete `+Timedata.Dummy+` in the Apache Felix Web Console of the "
"Backend (`+http://<host>:8079/system/console/configMgr+`) and create "
"`+Timedata.InfluxDB+` with the URL `+http://openems-influxdb:8086+` and the "
"token from `+influx auth list+` as ApiKey."
msgstr ""
"Danach in der Apache Felix Web Console des Backends (`+http://<host>:8079/"
"system/console/configMgr+`) `+Timedata.Dummy+` löschen und "
"`+Timedata.InfluxDB+` mit der URL `+http://openems-influxdb:8086+` und dem "
"Token aus `+influx auth list+` als ApiKey anlegen."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting an Edge to the Backend"
msgstr "Edge mit dem Backend verbinden"

#. type: #sec-connecting-an-edge-to-the-backend
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"On the Edge, create the component “Controller Api Backend” "
"(`+ctrlBackend0+`) with Uri `+ws://<docker-host>:8081+` (Backend-Edge, not "
"Backend) and the Apikey of the Edge from `+metadata.json+`. If the Edge runs "
"in the same Compose project, `+ws://openems-backend-edge:8081+` is possible."
msgstr ""
"Auf der Edge die Komponente „Controller Api Backend“ (`+ctrlBackend0+`) "
"anlegen, mit der Uri `+ws://<docker-host>:8081+` (Backend-Edge, nicht "
"Backend) und dem Apikey der Edge aus `+metadata.json+`. Läuft die Edge im "
"selben Compose-Projekt, ist `+ws://openems-backend-edge:8081+` möglich."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware access from the Edge container"
msgstr "Hardware-Zugriff aus dem Edge-Container"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Connection\n"
"| In the container\n"
"| Remark\n"
"\n"
"| Modbus/TCP, HTTP devices in the LAN\n"
"| works via the Docker bridge network\n"
"| Outgoing connections to the LAN do not need a port release.\n"
"| Modbus RTU via USB-RS485\n"
"| pass the device through: `+devices: [\"/dev/ttyUSB0:/dev/ttyUSB0\"]+`\n"
"| The user `+abc+` needs permissions on the device, e.g. via `+group_add+` with the GID of the group `+dialout+` of the host or matching `+PUID+`/`+PGID+`. The native Linux library of jSerialComm 2.11.4 is built against glibc, while Alpine uses musl. Neither the Edge Dockerfile nor the linuxserver base image installs the compatibility layer `+gcompat+`. Check with `+apk info -e gcompat+` in the container and install it if necessary.\n"
"| Devices that address the Edge (Modbus/TCP API, port 502)\n"
"| publish the port\n"
"| see <<sec-modbus-tcp,Modbus/TCP>>\n"
"| Discovery via broadcast/mDNS\n"
"| usually not in the bridge network\n"
"| If necessary `+network_mode: host+`; the `+ports+` entries are then omitted.\n"
"| GPIO, I²C, relays on the device itself\n"
"| only by passing the devices through\n"
"| \n"
msgstr ""
"| Anbindung\n"
"| Im Container\n"
"| Bemerkung\n"
"\n"
"| Modbus/TCP, HTTP-Geräte (Shelly, Wallboxen, Wechselrichter im LAN)\n"
"| funktioniert über das Bridge-Netz von Docker\n"
"| Ausgehende Verbindungen ins LAN brauchen keine Portfreigabe.\n"
"| Modbus RTU über USB-RS485\n"
"| Gerät durchreichen: `+devices: [\"/dev/ttyUSB0:/dev/ttyUSB0\"]+`\n"
"| Der Benutzer `+abc+` braucht Rechte auf das Gerät, z. B. über `+group_add+` mit der GID der Gruppe `+dialout+` des Hosts oder passende `+PUID+`/`+PGID+`. Die native Linux-Bibliothek der seriellen Bibliothek jSerialComm 2.11.4 ist gegen glibc gebaut (`+libc.so.6+`, Symbolversionen `+GLIBC_2.x+`). Alpine verwendet musl. Weder das Edge-Dockerfile noch das linuxserver-Basisimage installiert die Kompatibilitätsschicht `+gcompat+`. Im Container mit `+apk info -e gcompat+` prüfen und sie bei Bedarf nachinstallieren.\n"
"| Geräte, die die Edge ansprechen (z. B. Modbus-Slave-Schnittstelle der Edge, Port 502)\n"
"| Port veröffentlichen\n"
"| `+ports: [\"502:502\"]+`; Einzelheiten unter <<sec-modbus-tcp,Modbus/TCP>>.\n"
"| Erkennung per Broadcast/mDNS\n"
"| im Bridge-Netz in der Regel nicht\n"
"| Gegebenenfalls `+network_mode: host+`; dann entfallen die `+ports+`-Einträge.\n"
"| GPIO, I²C, Relais am Gerät selbst\n"
"| nur mit Durchreichen der Geräte\n"
"| \n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The time of the Edge comes from the host. For correct daily values and "
"tariffs, the host must be synchronized via NTP."
msgstr ""
"Die Uhrzeit der Edge kommt vom Host. Für korrekte Tageswerte und Tarife muss "
"der Host per NTP synchronisiert sein."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus/TCP"
msgstr "Modbus/TCP"

#. type: #sec-modbus-tcp
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid "Two directions have to be distinguished:"
msgstr "Zwei Richtungen sind zu unterscheiden:"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Direction\n"
"| Component\n"
"| Docker\n"
"\n"
"| Edge reads devices in the LAN (Edge is master)\n"
"| `+Bridge.Modbus.Tcp+` with IP and port of the device\n"
"| Nothing necessary; outgoing connections go through the bridge network\n"
"| Others read the Edge (Edge is slave)\n"
"| `+Controller.Api.ModbusTcp.ReadOnly+` or `+.ReadWrite+`\n"
"| publish the port\n"
msgstr ""
"| Richtung\n"
"| Komponente\n"
"| Docker\n"
"\n"
"| Edge liest Geräte im LAN (Edge ist Master)\n"
"| `+Bridge.Modbus.Tcp+` („Bridge Modbus/TCP“) mit IP und Port des Geräts; der Gerätetreiber verweist im Feld Modbus-ID auf die Bridge (z. B. `+modbus0+`)\n"
"| Nichts nötig; ausgehende Verbindungen gehen über das Bridge-Netz\n"
"| Andere lesen die Edge (Edge ist Slave)\n"
"| `+Controller.Api.ModbusTcp.ReadOnly+` bzw. `+.ReadWrite+`\n"
"| Port veröffentlichen\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Defaults of the slave interface according to the code (`+CommonConfig+`): "
"port 502 (`+DEFAULT_PORT+`), components `+_sum+`, at most 5 simultaneous "
"connections (`+DEFAULT_MAX_CONCURRENT_CONNECTIONS+`)."
msgstr ""
"Voreinstellungen der Slave-Schnittstelle laut Code (`+CommonConfig+`): Port "
"502 (`+DEFAULT_PORT+`), Komponenten `+_sum+`, höchstens 5 gleichzeitige "
"Verbindungen (`+DEFAULT_MAX_CONCURRENT_CONNECTIONS+`)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"A host port can only be assigned once; if several Edges run on one host, "
"each gets its own host port (e.g. `+5020:502+`). New ports are only adopted "
"by a recreated container (`+docker compose up -d <service>+`); `+restart+` "
"is not sufficient."
msgstr ""
"Ein Host-Port kann nur einmal vergeben werden; laufen mehrere Edges auf "
"einem Host, bekommt jede einen eigenen Host-Port (z. B. `+5020:502+`). Neue "
"Ports übernimmt erst ein neu erstellter Container (`+docker compose up -d "
"<dienst>+`), `+restart+` reicht nicht."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Port below 1024: The Edge runs as `+abc+` in the container. Docker sets "
"`+net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=0+` in the container if the container "
"has its own network (not `+network_mode: host+`) and the kernel knows the "
"setting. With `+network_mode: host+`, the setting of the host applies. If "
"“Permission denied” appears in the log, set e.g. port 1502 in the component "
"and publish it as `+5020:1502+`."
msgstr ""
"Port unter 1024: Die Edge läuft im Container als `+abc+`, Port 502 liegt "
"unter 1024. Docker setzt im Container "
"`+net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=0+`, wenn der Container ein eigenes "
"Netzwerk hat (nicht `+network_mode: host+`) und der Kernel die Einstellung "
"kennt. Mit `+network_mode: host+` gilt die Einstellung des Hosts. Erscheint "
"im Log „Permission denied“, in der Komponente z. B. Port 1502 einstellen und "
"als `+5020:1502+` veröffentlichen."

#. type: Title ====
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting if the Edge does not read a device"
msgstr "Fehlersuche, wenn die Edge ein Gerät nicht liest"

#. type: #sec-troubleshooting-if-the-edge-does-not-read-a-device
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Narrow down step by step whether it is due to the network, the container or "
"the device:"
msgstr ""
"Schrittweise eingrenzen, ob es am Netz, am Container oder am Gerät liegt "
"(Platzhalter `+<IP>+`, Bridge-ID und Komponenten-IDs ersetzen):"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 1. Does the host reach the device?\n"
"nc -zv -w 3 <IP> 502\n"
msgstr ""
"# 1. Host erreicht das Gerät?\n"
"nc -zv -w 3 <IP> 502\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 2. Does the container reach the device?\n"
"docker exec openems_edge bash -c 'timeout 3 bash -c \"</dev/tcp/<IP>/502\" && echo open || echo closed'\n"
msgstr ""
"# 2. Container erreicht das Gerät?\n"
"docker exec openems_edge bash -c 'timeout 3 bash -c \"</dev/tcp/<IP>/502\" && echo offen || echo zu'\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 3. Error messages of the Bridge (without the lines of the debug log Controller)\n"
"docker compose logs --tail=2000 openems-edge | grep -v ctrlDebugLog | grep -i -E 'modbus|<bridge-id>' | tail -40\n"
msgstr ""
"# 3. Fehlermeldungen der Bridge (ohne die Zeilen des Debug-Log-Controllers)\n"
"docker compose logs --tail=2000 openems-edge | grep -v ctrlDebugLog | grep -i -E 'modbus|<bridge-id>' | tail -40\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 4. Modbus request without Edge, directly from the host (package mbpoll)\n"
"mbpoll -m tcp -a 1 -t 4 -r 40001 -c 2 -o 5 -1 <IP>\n"
msgstr ""
"# 4. Modbus-Anfrage ohne Edge, direkt vom Host (Paket mbpoll)\n"
"mbpoll -m tcp -a 1 -t 4 -r 40001 -c 2 -o 5 -1 <IP>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The lines of `+ctrlDebugLog0+` only show states (e.g. “Modbus Communication "
"failed”). The Bridge writes the actual error message as `+ERROR "
"[e.modbus.api.task.AbstractTask] Execute failed …+`. If this is not "
"sufficient, temporarily set “Log-Verbosity” in the Bridge to "
"`+READS_AND_WRITES+` and reset it afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Die Zeilen von `+ctrlDebugLog0+` zeigen nur Zustände (z. B. „Modbus "
"Communication failed“). Die eigentliche Fehlermeldung schreibt die Bridge "
"als `+ERROR [e.modbus.api.task.AbstractTask] Execute failed …+`. Reicht das "
"nicht, in der Bridge „Log-Verbosity“ vorübergehend auf `+READS_AND_WRITES+` "
"stellen und danach zurücksetzen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"“Connection refused” or errors already with `+nc+`: network, firewall, port "
"or Modbus switched off on the device."
msgstr ""
"„Connection refused“ oder Fehler schon bei `+nc+`: Netz, Firewall, Port oder "
"Modbus am Gerät abgeschaltet."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"“Socket timeout reading response - Read timed out”: the TCP connection is "
"up, but the device does not respond in time. The Bridge waits for a fixed "
"**500 ms** (`+AbstractModbusBridge.DEFAULT_TIMEOUT+`, set in "
"`+BridgeModbusTcpImpl+`, not configurable). If the device responds more "
"slowly, every request fails, even though the address and Unit-ID are correct."
msgstr ""
"„Socket timeout reading response - Read timed out“: Die TCP-Verbindung "
"steht, das Gerät antwortet aber nicht rechtzeitig. Die Bridge wartet fest "
"**500 ms** (`+AbstractModbusBridge.DEFAULT_TIMEOUT+`, gesetzt in "
"`+BridgeModbusTcpImpl+`, nicht konfigurierbar). Antwortet das Gerät "
"langsamer, scheitert jede Abfrage, obwohl Adresse und Unit-ID stimmen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"`+mbpoll+` counts registers from 1: `+-r 40001+` corresponds to address "
"40000 of the Bridge. For SunSpec devices, this request returns `+21365 "
"28243+` (`+0x5375 0x6E53+` = “SunS”), which confirms reachability and Unit-"
"ID. `+-o+` extends the waiting time."
msgstr ""
"`+mbpoll+` zählt Register ab 1: `+-r 40001+` entspricht Adresse 40000 der "
"Bridge. Bei SunSpec-Geräten liefert diese Abfrage `+21365 28243+` (`+0x5375 "
"0x6E53+` = „SunS“); damit sind Erreichbarkeit und Unit-ID belegt. Mit `+-o+` "
"lässt sich die Wartezeit verlängern."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Development workflows"
msgstr "Entwicklungs-Workflows"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Goal\n"
"| Procedure\n"
"\n"
"| Test your own change as in operation\n"
"| Build the image from your fork, use it in the Compose file, keep the same volumes.\n"
"| Debug the Edge in Eclipse, UI in the container\n"
"| `+tools/docker/ui/docker-compose.yml+`, see xref:ui/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy the UI with Docker].\n"
"| Debug the Edge in the container\n"
"| `pass:c[EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError -agentlib:jdwp=transport=dt_socket,server=y,suspend=n,address=*:5005]` and publish port 5005; in Eclipse “Remote Java Application” to `+<host>:5005+` (not tried out with this image).\n"
"| Test only a new JAR, without an image build\n"
"| `+./gradlew buildEdge+` locally, place the JAR over `+/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar+` via bind mount.\n"
"| Simulate several Edges\n"
"| Several Edge services with their own volumes and different host ports in one Compose file; each with its own Apikey on the Backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"| Ziel\n"
"| Vorgehen\n"
"\n"
"| Eigene Änderung testen, wie im Betrieb\n"
"| Image aus dem eigenen Stand bauen, in der Compose-Datei verwenden, gleiche Volumes behalten.\n"
"| Edge in Eclipse debuggen, UI im Container\n"
"| `+tools/docker/ui/docker-compose.yml+`, siehe xref:latest@ui/deploy/docker.adoc[Deploy the UI with Docker].\n"
"| Edge im Container debuggen\n"
"| `pass:c[EXTRA_JVM_OPTS=-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError -agentlib:jdwp=transport=dt_socket,server=y,suspend=n,address=*:5005]` und Port 5005 veröffentlichen; in Eclipse „Remote Java Application“ auf `+<host>:5005+`. (Mit diesem Image nicht ausprobiert.)\n"
"| Nur ein neues JAR testen, ohne Image-Build\n"
"| `+./gradlew buildEdge+` lokal, JAR per Bind-Mount über `+/opt/openems/openems-edge.jar+` legen.\n"
"| Mehrere Edges simulieren\n"
"| Mehrere Edge-Dienste mit eigenen Volumes und unterschiedlichen Host-Ports in einer Compose-Datei; jede mit eigenem Apikey am Backend.\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "Ressourcen"

#. type: #sec-resources
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"The Edge targets weak hardware (about 1 GB RAM). Without `+-Xmx+`, the JVM "
"in the container by default takes a quarter of the memory visible to the "
"container as the heap limit. On a host with a lot of RAM, it is advisable to "
"set the heap with `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+` or a memory limit (`+mem_limit+`)."
msgstr ""
"Die Edge zielt auf schwache Hardware (etwa 1 GB RAM). Ohne `+-Xmx+` nimmt "
"die JVM im Container standardmäßig ein Viertel des für den Container "
"sichtbaren Speichers als Heap-Obergrenze. Auf einem Host mit viel RAM "
"empfiehlt es sich, den Heap mit `+EXTRA_JVM_OPTS+` oder ein Speicherlimit "
"(`+mem_limit+`) festzulegen."

#. type: #sec-resources
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
msgid ""
"Backend and InfluxDB need significantly more depending on the number of "
"Edges. There are no figures for this in the code or documentation."
msgstr ""
"Backend und InfluxDB brauchen je nach Zahl der Edges deutlich mehr. Zahlen "
"dazu stehen weder im Code noch in der Doku."

